by replacing each pixel with its matching top stencil.\n  25: \n  26:     Input structure\n  27:     The input has a top legend and a lower dense color grid, separated by blank rows.\n  28:     The legend contains left-to-right 2x2 color swatches and, to their right,\n  29:     the same number of square neutral-color stencil masks.\n  30: \n  31:     Rule\n  32:     Pair the swatches and stencil masks by left-to-right order. For every pixel in\n  33:     the lower color grid, paste the paired stencil mask as one output block,\n  34:     recoloring the mask pixels with that pixel's color and leaving mask holes as bg.\n  35: \n  36:     Key insight\n  37:     The lower grid is not copied directly; it is an index grid whose colors select\n  38:     the stencil shape from the legend, so each input pixel becomes one square block.\n  39:     \"\"\"\n  40:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n  41:     bg = get_bg(g)\n  42: \n  43:     row_runs = _runs(np.any(g != bg, axis=1))\n  44:     assert len(row_runs) == 2\n  45:     (top_r0, top_r1), (pattern_r0, pattern_r1) = row_runs\n  46:     assert top_r0 == 0\n  47: \n  48:     stencil_size = top_r1 - top_r0 + 1\n  49:     top = g[top_r0 : top_r1 + 1, :]\n  50:     lower = g[pattern_r0 : pattern_r1 + 1, :]\n  51: \n  52:     pattern_box = bbox(lower != bg)\n  53:     assert pattern_box is not None\n  54:     pr0, pc0, pr1, pc1 = pattern_box\n  55:     assert pr0 == 0 and pr1 == lower.shape[0] - 1\n  56:     pattern = lower[:, pc0 : pc1 + 1]\n  57:     assert np.all(pattern != bg)\n  58:     pattern_colors = set(map(int, np.unique(pattern)))\n  59: \n  60:     top_colors = set(map(int, np.unique(top))) - {bg}\n  61:     neutral_colors = top_colors - pattern_colors\n  62:     assert len(neutral_colors) == 1\n  63:     neutral = next(iter(neutral_colors))\n  64: \n  65:     swatches = []\n  66:     for comp in find_components(top, bg=bg, colors=pattern_colors):\n  67:         r0, c0, r1, c1 = comp[\"bbox\"]\n  68:         assert