 \n  22:     Input structure\n  23:     - The grid has full-width and full-height bars of one separator color, dividing it into rectangular cells.\n  24:     - Most cells contain a repeating multicolor pattern, while a contiguous rectangle of cells is solid monochrome.\n  25: \n  26:     Rule\n  27:     - Split the input into lattice cells using the full separator rows and columns.\n  28:     - Keep the cells whose full interior is one color, crop to their occupied rectangle, and output those colors.\n  29: \n  30:     Key insight\n  31:     - The periodic pattern is noise; only completely solid lattice cells encode the reduced output grid.\n  32:     \"\"\"\n  33:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n  34:     h, w = g.shape\n  35: \n  36:     row_colors = {int(g[r, 0]) for r in range(h) if np.all(g[r, :] == g[r, 0])}\n  37:     col_colors = {int(g[0, c]) for c in range(w) if np.all(g[:, c] == g[0, c])}\n  38:     sep_colors = row_colors & col_colors\n  39:     assert len(sep_colors) == 1, \"there must be exactly one row/column separator color\"\n  40:     sep = next(iter(sep_colors))\n  41:     assert row_colors == {sep}, \"all full rows must be separator rows\"\n  42:     assert col_colors == {sep}, \"all full columns must be separator columns\"\n  43: \n  44:     sep_rows = [r for r in range(h) if np.all(g[r, :] == sep)]\n  45:     sep_cols = [c for c in range(w) if np.all(g[:, c] == sep)]\n  46:     assert sep_rows and sep_cols, \"separator lattice must have rows and columns\"\n  47: \n  48:     row_bands = _bands(h, sep_rows)\n  49:     col_bands = _bands(w, sep_cols)\n  50: \n  51:     solid_cells = {}\n  52:     for ri, (r0, r1) in enumerate(row_bands):\n  53:         for ci, (c0, c1) in enumerate(col_bands):\n  54:             cell = g[r0 : r1 + 1, c0 : c1 + 1]\n  55:             if np.all(cell == cell[0, 0]):\n  56:                 solid_cells[(ri, ci)] = int(cell[0, 0])\n  57:     assert solid_cells, \"must contain at least one solid lattice cell\"\n  58: